### Project Scope
Inclusions:
- Migration of existing GAMBAS code to Python, including all business critical logic.
- Streamlining the process by optimizing outdated logic and features and re-engineering of the pipeline to enhance efficiency.
- Orchestration of fragmented functionalities into a seamless ecosystem.
- Containerizing new pipeline using Docker.
- Deployment of the pipeline to AWS with properly configured infrastructure (ECS/Fargate, Lambda, EFS, S3, ACM, Route 53, and Ocelot) for scalability and security.
- Conducting thorough testing (unit, integration, and user acceptance) of the migrated application.
- Creating comprehensive and clear code documentation and user documentation.

### Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)
Task 0: Project Plan Creation (Week -7)
- Create a feasible project plan to be reviewed and approved by sponsors and stakeholders.

Task 1: Requirement Analysis and Infrastructure Logic Mapping (Week -6 to -2)
- Gather core requirements for the new system through document reviews, including relevant regulatory guidance and raw GAMBAS code.
- Map the underlying logic within and between the core functionalities to lay the foundation for the infrastructure.
- Create a presentation with compiled information for onboarding and future reference, to be shared with stakeholders.

Task 2: Migration Planning (Week -1 to 2)
- Create a migration strategy and timeline, including risk assessment and resource allocation. 
- Onboard the developer with the production project example, regulatory requirements and legacy logic mapping.
- Set up access to GAMBAS code, dev/testing server, and GitHub & AWS environment.

Task 3: Code Migration, Optimization, Modularization, and Documentation (Week 3-15)
- Streamline and optimize the logic, optimizing legacy features.
- Migrate the core GAMBAS code to Python, with defined input and output that meet regulatory requirements.
- Modularize the code for maintainability and future feature additions.
- Document the code for continuous development and maintenance.
- Perform unit testing, integration testing.
- Engage stakeholders regularly on the development progress (weekly or biweekly).
- Commit all code to Bayer GitHub.

Task 4: Code Containerization (Week 16-17)
- Put migrated code into Docker containers for deployment.

Task 5: AWS Setup and Deployment (Week 18-20)
- Configure AWS environment (ECS/Fargate, Lambda, EFS, S3, ACM, and Route 53) for deployment.
- Deploy the application on AWS and ensure all services are operational, verified by a checklist.
- Conduct performance and security testing of the AWS setup.

Task 7: Production Testing and Feedback (Week 21-22)
- Complete 2-3 end-to-end tests with the productionized projects, and collect feedback from the end users.

Task 8: Improvement, Post-Deployment Support (Week 23-24)
- Conduct bug fixing and software improvements based on feedback. 
- Provide support to the bifx team with Q&A.

### Resources
- One professional contractor for six months
- AWS Infrastructure: $2000 (ECS and EFS for testing)

### Risk Management
*Potential Risks* 
- Challenges in understanding the dependencies and data post-processing of the inter-wiring multi-year legacy code, potentially leading to delays.
- Complexity in corporate cloud landscope and compatibility issues of AWS features and company firewall, which may affect deployment.
- Potential delays in gaining access to needed resources.

*Mitigation Strategies*
- Conduct a thorough analysis of both regulatory requirements and the GAMBAS codebase before migration.
- Seek out expertise in the corporate AWS community when encounter compatibility issues.
- Plan for access request as soon as onboarding starts if not prior.

*Communication Plan*
- Meet weekly to discuss progress and challenges, assess performance against objectives, and adjust plans as necessary.  
- Update the bifx team weekly in the production meeting (5-10 min) with a summary of progress and any challenges encountered.
- Share monthly progress update with key stakeholders, with two presentations (middle and final)
- Report any unexpected delays and/or additional resource requirements to the sponsors.
- Document updates and user guides, ensuring all stakeholders have access to the latest information.

### Monitoring and Evaluation
*KPIs*
- Successful migration of all core functionalities (tracked via testing results).
- Achieve a 70% reduction in manual software interactions, improving user friendliness and minimize new user training overhead.
- Application performance metrics post-deployment (response time, uptime, failure rate, etc.).
- Cost savings achieved through AWS optimization (may be irrelevant since we’re paying little as of now).
- Code modularization and documentation (module reusability rate, number of module dependencies, documentation coverage, github copilot scoring).

